OrionLayer open fix 103 — colonists to any colony of the player
===============================================================

Work order 316 (Data, 20 October 2026: "moving colonists between planets
did not work ... make it work as the original does"; and 315's P8: "The
original moves colonists between colonies from the Colonies list,
including to another star by freighters ... Build it as the original's,
transcribed."). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on
top of open fix 102; commit 96c39753. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/ext/ (ext_api.cpp, ext_server.cpp, ext_server.h), which is built only
with ORION2RE_EXT.

Open fix 92's MSG_SETTLE_POPS settles colonists of the colony screen's
colony in another colony at the same star, all or none, and refuses any
pop that would make the original ask a question. The original's
COLMOVE::Send_Cluster_ (colmove.cpp:145-531 in the 1.60 source) does more:
from the colony screen's transport popup (COLXPORT::Xport_Popup_,
colony_main.cpp:1068-1076) and from the Colonies list (colsum.cpp:869,
:909) it sends them to any colony of the player, by freighters to another
star with an ETA, asking "unavailable for N turns, are you sure?" (E 0x209)
and "go on past the limit?" (E 0x205 / 0x203, 0x206 / 0x204), settling
colonist by colonist up to the first that may not go, and says what it did
in "Settlers Failed." and "Settlers Depart" boxes.

The long form: two bytes after the pop list — uint8 answers (bit 0 YES to
"go on past the limit?", bit 1 YES to the ETA question), int8 job (-1
keeps it; 0-2 the job each colonist takes first, as Give_Colonist_New_Job_
gives it for a transfer, its three refusals checked without their box).
Accepted on SCREEN_COLONY for the colony it shows and on
SCREEN_COLONY_SUMMARY for any colony of the player. Each pop is asked
about with SETTLER::Pop_Tries_To_Settle_ and moved with Settle_Pop_, both
unchanged; a pop the original would ask about without the matching YES,
or a refusal, ends the walk; whoever did not go is assigned again (the
client keeps them in its hand). Col_Calc_Wrapper for both colonies, then,
when someone went, Colony_Calculation for both (colmove.cpp:476-479,
:524-525). The short form is unchanged.

The block: "STLR" on SCREEN_COLONY and SCREEN_COLONY_SUMMARY, after MREL's
place — a version byte (1), uint16 the long-form commands taken, int16
source and destination colony, uint8 listed, uint8 settled, uint8 why it
stopped (0 none, 1 refused, 2 a question without its YES, 3 a job refusal,
4 the list refused), uint8 the job refusal, uint8 the extra notice, then
the fifteen bytes of s_settler_settle_result for the last pop asked about.
Read only.

